{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/369207-ritual-of-sacred-rebirth-on-embraced-kinfolk","id":369207,"title":"Ritual of Sacred Rebirth on Embraced Kinfolk?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-13T17:42:40-08:00","id":369207,"title":"Ritual of Sacred Rebirth on Embraced Kinfolk?","content":"I'm just curious. Is it a possibility? And if it is would such a creature be subject to the &quot;normal&quot; disadvantages of being an abomination?<br /> The ritual is of the Wyrm and seeing as vampires are wyrm-creatures I figured it might not be an obstacle but I would like some input.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4003-kristviljan","name":"Kristviljan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4003_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T17:51:35-08:00","id":369220,"title":"","content":"I think no one ever thought it, but (if the ritual works) you will probably create a whole new type of monster, a sort of Uber-Abomination with all the power of the Abomination without his flaws, because the actual access to the spirit-world was given to him AFTER the Embrace, would be a super abomination, perfectly half-breed to both the Cainite and Garou world...<br /> <br /> would be... a Perfect Metis \u00b0_________\u00b0","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","user":"Ryoga84","date":". 01-13-2015, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T17:59:17-08:00","id":369229,"title":"","content":"This is addressed in the Storytellers handbook (revised) I believe and it says that rites will not work for vampires. and specifically notes even Wyrm rites, and mentions the Rite of Sacred Rebirth by name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T18:16:54-08:00","id":369241,"title":"","content":"I see, does that apply for all rites or only those performed by a vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4003-kristviljan","name":"Kristviljan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4003_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T19:54:32-08:00","id":369334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kristviljan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/369207-ritual-of-sacred-rebirth-on-embraced-kinfolk?p=369241#post369241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see, does that apply for all rites or only those performed by a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what the question is here. the book states that vampires cannot perform (well enact might be a better word) any rites. Spirits won't answer their call. Mind you, this is from the Werewolf Storytellers Guide. If you use the Vampire books, it might allow for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T20:19:05-08:00","id":369353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/369207-ritual-of-sacred-rebirth-on-embraced-kinfolk?p=369334#post369334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure what the question is here. the book states that vampires cannot perform (well enact might be a better word) any rites. Spirits won't answer their call. Mind you, this is from the Werewolf Storytellers Guide. If you use the Vampire books, it might allow for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he's asking what if Werewolf (Black Spiral I guess) performed the ritual on the Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T20:22:52-08:00","id":369354,"title":"","content":"I don't really agree that this is the way it should be, but all text indicators that the Rite must be performed on oneself. So no one can perform the Rite of Sacred Rebirth for someone else. That leads to the odd situation of way too many ex-kinfolk skindancers with a 5 in rituals (which should take years and years, possibly decades of study).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T13:12:16-08:00","id":371384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/369207-ritual-of-sacred-rebirth-on-embraced-kinfolk?p=369354#post369354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really agree that this is the way it should be, but all text indicators that the Rite must be performed on oneself. So no one can perform the Rite of Sacred Rebirth for someone else. That leads to the odd situation of way too many ex-kinfolk skindancers with a 5 in rituals (which should take years and years, possibly decades of study).</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a good point... I think the Rite of Sacred Rebirth needs to be difficult, but the idea that all Skin Dancers need 5 dots in rituals is rather nuts. There might be a handful of individuals with that level of spiritual knowledge, but requiring each and every child of Minotaur to be among the best ritual magic users on the planet is absurd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T18:07:45-08:00","id":371620,"title":"","content":"I was hoping that they would've changed how the ritual worked when the Skinner SAS came out, but it didn't happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T16:46:46-08:00","id":373072,"title":"","content":"Is it absurd? I thought about this for a few days, and I honestly do not feel it is absurd. It might have been an oversight, but what if it wasn't? Rituals 5 isn't exactly useless... and the core theme of a Skin Dancer is someone who has the knowledge and ability to steal a sacred gift. Is Rituals 5 that rare, or are Skin Dancers that common?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T16:52:18-08:00","id":373080,"title":"","content":"I'm not that experienced with the Skinner side of things, but I kind of figured that discovering and crafting the ritual in the first place would certainly need five dots...but sharing it with someone else, more like three. If you are going to induct someone into the Skin Dancers, then even if they perform the ritual themselves, they don't need to steal or rebuild it out of whole cloth; you can advise them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T17:22:02-08:00","id":373103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/369207-ritual-of-sacred-rebirth-on-embraced-kinfolk?p=373080#post373080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not that experienced with the Skinner side of things, but I kind of figured that discovering and crafting the ritual in the first place would certainly need five dots...but sharing it with someone else, more like three. If you are going to induct someone into the Skin Dancers, then even if they perform the ritual themselves, they don't need to steal or rebuild it out of whole cloth; you can advise them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't mean the Rite itself, but rather the Garou pelts required to make it work... stealing the sacred gift of being a werewolf from Gaia herself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T09:49:54-08:00","id":387458,"title":"","content":"I have a better related question... Embraced Kinfolk with Spirit Manipulation from Guide to the Camarilla at Four, maybe Three could also probably duplicate or perform the Ritual that way. If the Ritual is used, the path would allow a much easier time of -making- the spirits do what you need them to do if it is a problem of not being able to get the spirits to answer the call. Would that not be a viable work around to the problem?<br /> <br /> If sticking to just what is in the V20 book, Spiritus is a likely answer at least fluff wise, or Mytherceria 8 (to be no longer a vampire for a day as you lose all blessings and drawbacks of being a Kindred!). Gift of Life (5th dot of The Corpse in the Monster) is a stretch, but might allow the ritual to be performed. Mayaparisatya (Chimestry 9) might also be able to the bend the rules enough to get it to work. Soul Mask (Obfuscate 6) might also be able to get around it if they are reacting to the aura the individual has to decided to not help, in which case so might the merit Deceptive Aura if the spirits could be fooled into thinking you are alive so they will work with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4881-veros","name":"Veros","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}